    'The excavation report first describes a house whose rooms were arranged around a central courtyard. It then notes that the largest room contains no hearth, while small exterior platforms show repeated ash deposits. The author proposes that cooking occurred outside and that the courtyard organized circulation rather than serving as the household’s primary work space. The evidence thus reverses an intuitive reading of the floor plan.',
