    'The essay opens with a familiar story about an inventor working alone in a workshop. It then follows the patent records, which name machinists, suppliers, and laboratory assistants absent from the story. The final paragraph does not deny the inventor’s creativity; it argues that the invention’s development is better understood as a networked process than as a solitary act.',
