    'The policy analyst begins by noting that a subsidy increased the number of households purchasing insulation. A later survey shows that many of those households installed less insulation than the program required, reducing the expected energy savings. The analyst concludes that uptake is an incomplete measure of policy effectiveness: participation must be paired with implementation quality.',
